<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Public Limited Company Registration?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p><strong>Definition:</strong> Incorporation under S.2(71) Companies Act 2013. Not a private company. Min 7 shareholders, 3 directors. Shares freely transferable. Can invite public subscription via prospectus. Registered via SPICe+ with RoC Delhi.</p><p><strong>Defining advantage:</strong> Only structure for IPO on BSE/NSE. Issue publicly tradeable debentures. Accept QIB investment. No private placement restrictions.</p><p><strong>For Delhi:</strong> Prerequisite for SEBI-approved DRHP. BSE SME listing requires 3-year audit track. NBFC licensing under S.45-IA RBI Act needs public company credibility.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Public Limited Company in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>Prospectus S.2(70):</strong> Document inviting public to subscribe to shares/debentures. SEBI-reviewed for listed companies.</p><p><strong>DRHP:</strong> Draft Red Herring Prospectus filed with SEBI before IPO. 3 years audited financials, risk factors per SEBI ICDR 2018.</p><p><strong>SEBI LODR 2015:</strong> Listing Obligations: 1/3 independent directors, audit committee, quarterly disclosures. Top 1000 = min 6 directors.</p><p><strong>RoC Delhi:</strong> IFCI Tower, 61 Nehru Place, New Delhi 110019. Issues COI with CIN format L/U[code]DL[year]PLC[number].</p>

                </div>
            </div>
